{
  "_comment": [
    "Sibling of layout/pex-array/pex.json and layout/pex-sampler-dff-assembled/",
    "pex.json, one level further up the hierarchy than either: extracts the",
    "fully-composed, DRC-clean and klt-lvs-MATCHING sampler_core GDS --",
    "layout/sampler_core/sampler_core.gds (264/264 devices, 152/152 nets",
    "against design/sampler_core.spice's own .subckt sampler_core; see that",
    "directory's README) -- with `klt extract --parasitics`, and rewrites the",
    "result the same way: layout/bin/pex-netlist.py is shared, unmodified,",
    "across every descriptor under layout/.",
    "",
    "cells[].ports is design/sampler_core.spice's own `.subckt sampler_core",
    "en1 en2 en3 en4 vddr1 vddr2 vddr3 vddr4 vdd vss clk rst_n raw_bit",
    "raw_valid ring_bit1 ring_bit2 ring_bit3 ring_bit4` port order.",
    "",
    "net_aliases below was built from layout/sampler_core/lvs.json's own",
    "net_correspondence array (the klt-lvs-verified layout<->reference net",
    "map from the whole-cell match that landed this GDS), not inferred from",
    "spelling -- every design-level name quoted here (xo, ro1-4, t1/t2,",
    "rn1-4, raw_bit/raw_valid/ring_bit1-4, and the six per-instance",
    "sampler_dff internal nets m/mb/mc/s/qb/clkb) is that JSON's own",
    "`reference` field for the matching `layout` entry, re-verified against a",
    "fresh `klt extract --parasitics` run over the same committed GDS (see",
    "this directory's README for the reproduction command and the full",
    "derivation, including why the raw_bit/raw_valid/ring_bit1-4 family",
    "needs six explicit entries instead of one base alias)."
  ],
